Statement: "The unenroll succeeded on the server; the error comes from parsing a response that has no body, so the API layer should treat 204 as success without calling res.json() rather than retry the request."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'True. 204 No Content means the request succeeded and the response has no content by definition (RFC 9110, section 15.3.5); the API log confirms the row was deleted. res.json() on an empty body rejects with a SyntaxError, so the UI reports an error for an action that worked, and a retry would send a second DELETE for nothing. The typed API layer handles this once: check the status first, return success with no data (or an empty list) for 204, and only parse a body that exists. The misconception is that any exception after fetch means the request failed.', 2, 5
